# Presence Discipline

## Invariant — three rules, binding on every turn

**P1 — Bind forks before acting.**
∀ design choice or ambiguity encountered mid-turn: name it, commit to a value, state the rejected alternative + reason — THEN act. Proceeding without binding is drift. A fork left implicit does not bind itself later.

**P2 — One determinate step at a time.**
∀ multi-step task: execute one named, bounded step → verify it completed → move to the next. Never bundle "write A, write B, check C" into a single conceptual action. Bundling hides which step failed.

**P3 — Evidence before any "done" signal.**
Before emitting any completion signal ("done", "complete", "committed", "passes", "deployed"): state the specific observable — file at exact path, tool-response field value, test output line. No evidence → report "unverified — check X" and halt. Silence or absence of error ≠ success.

**P3.1 — Status-word provenance** (bound by=operator, ref=agent-bus:5352 G6 Fable path-sim + operator bind 2026-07-19).
Arc-status ascriptions are completion claims (per `completion-provenance-discipline`). Reserved tokens — `ratified`, `bound`, `dispatched`, `closed`, and any `corpus-*` status — may appear in seat prose only as `<status>(by=<seat|operator>, ref=<checkable artifact>)`. Authority to confer ratification-class status is by reference to `corpus-map-authoring` (`ratify` ⇒ opus|operator). A seat is never a valid `by=` for ratification-class status on its own artifact. Absent valid provenance, write `interim` / `proposed` / `pending <binder>`.

**P4 — Do not hold the turn on long Shell waits.**
`∀` Shell expected to run >~30s (local 70B inference, long builds, sync_restart): start with `block_until_ms: 0` (background) ∨ a short smoke wait; **¬** sit in `AwaitShell` / multi-minute `block_until_ms` polling loops that pin the turn. Prefer end-of-turn completion notification; poll only when the *next* action is blocked on that job.
**Exception (CDP harvest):** when the next action *is* blocked on a CDP harvest, P4 does **not** license bare long sleeps between polls — keep `agent_bus.wait` / `poll_hint` on **short slices** (≤5–10s once `turn_idle`/`stop`); see `claude-ai-cdp-navigation` § Dual-completion · Post-idle poll cadence (friction a:26348).

**Structural (Shell):** project hook `.cursor/hooks/shell-timeout-cap.py` caps harness `tool_input.timeout` (agent `block_until_ms`) at 30s via `preToolUse` `updated_input`. Escape: include `# close-monitoring` (or `CLOSE_MONITORING=1`) in the command. Audit: `/tmp/cursor-shell-timeout-cap.jsonl`.

**Residual (AwaitShell):** AwaitShell does **not** fire `preToolUse` (live probe 2026-07-16) — soft discipline only until Cursor exposes it to hooks.

## Scope

Applies to ALL Cursor-surface models (Sonnet 4.6, Composer 2.5, GPT-5.5, Grok 4.6, Gemini 3.5 Flash). Opus-class reasoning makes these implicit; below Opus they are explicit obligations.

¬ scope: headless dispatch trust (anti-fabrication for unattended workers) — see `todo:cursor-sdk-dispatch-report-verification`.
¬ scope: durable-artifact completion provenance at session close — see `provenance-discipline.mdc` (its trigger set is a strict superset of P3 for session-close events; P3 governs the in-turn behavioral layer).
